# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: Preserve the optional take decision after each card exiled by Tainted Pact.
# Forcing: The ordered library has three distinct choices followed by a duplicate Forest.
# AI behavior: The opponent has no hand or battlefield and makes no relevant decision.
# Failure modes:
#   WIN = the scripted acceptance line observes its chosen hand/exile result and continued play.
#   LOSE = a card is taken without consent or duplicate-name termination is ignored.
#   TIMEOUT = the optional decision or subsequent priority cannot advance.
# Card roles:
#   Tainted Pact supplies the repeated optional transfer.
#   Forest, Island, Mountain, Forest supply the exact choice and duplicate sequence.
#   Swamps pay for the spell; Ornithopter proves the next cast; Plains keeps a land play available.
# Protocol path: Cast, OptionalActionMessage/Resp for each distinct card, then ordinary priority.

[metadata]
Name:Tainted Pact Optional Take
Goal:Survive
Turns:5
Difficulty:Easy
Description:Take the first card, decline twice and take Mountain, or decline until the duplicate Forest stops the effect.

